WEBVTT

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.600
Stronghold only has 3000 attack 
points when Green Gadget,

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:23.640
Yellow Gadget and Red 
Gadget are on the field.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.500
Without all three, it has 0 attack points.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:28.640
I see victory!

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:33.480
I discard Shooting Star 
Bow - Ceal from my hand

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:36.580
to activate the spell card 
Tribute to the Doomed!

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:40.180
I destroy Green Gadget!

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:45.420
Stronghold's attack points become 0!

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:49.480
Then I equip Axe of Despair!

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:53.130
Ancient Gear Soldier's 
attack points become 2300!

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:58.320
Go, Ancient Gear Soldier!

00:00:58.320 --> 00:00:59.840
Attack Stronghold!

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:14.000
We did it!

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:16.390
Well done, Bruno!

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:18.990
We have to check the fingerprint quickly!

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:25.230
That's...

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:26.160
Do you know him?

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:29.200
He's the Vice Director of the 
Public Maintenance Department.

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:31.150
It's Yeager.

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:55.080
Every time you're hurt, you can become kinder

00:01:55.440 --> 00:02:00.610
Stand up and you'll understand strength

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:05.090
Don't look back and keep going

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:10.920
Both the past and the future 
are connected to the present

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:15.900
There's no need to fear

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:23.570
I'll keep telling you that you're not alone

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:29.580
The passionate emotions in your heart

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:35.350
Streak to the infinite future

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:40.750
Dreams surpass their limits

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:48.860
And will lead you to a bright place

00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:21.400
Plan to Capture Yeager!

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:24.550
Public Maintenance Department's 
Vice Director Yeager.

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:28.480
He's the one who stole our program?

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:31.120
He's never come here before.

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:33.670
But since his fingerprint 
is here, there's no doubt.

00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:35.690
Why would a high-ranked official steal?

00:03:35.690 --> 00:03:39.120
Is he planning to sell it and make money?

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:43.180
I don't know, so we have to ask him directly.

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:49.130
That program is worth a lot to the robber.

00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:52.840
If he's going to give it to someone, 
he won't transmit the data.

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:54.850
He'll hand it over in person.

00:03:54.850 --> 00:03:55.800
You're right.

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:58.570
That means he'll be acting solo.

00:03:58.570 --> 00:04:01.190
That's when we'll catch him!

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:02.920
It's decided.

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:12.230
That program is our bond to 
make our dreams come true,

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:13.930
Yusei...

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:17.900
We must retrieve our bond!

00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:29.540
As you ordered, I stole their program.

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:32.530
They better not find out 
that you're the thief.

00:04:32.530 --> 00:04:33.980
Of course not!

00:04:33.980 --> 00:04:38.480
I wouldn't make the mistake of 
leaving any evidence behind!

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:39.740
Fine.

00:04:39.740 --> 00:04:42.160
Bring it here immediately.

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:44.430
Personally?

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:47.140
Of course!  Bring it quickly!

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:49.870
Understood!

00:04:57.540 --> 00:04:58.720
He's here!

00:04:58.720 --> 00:04:59.740
Okay!

00:05:10.730 --> 00:05:13.890
Head towards #72 in B Sector.

00:05:13.890 --> 00:05:15.150
That's...

00:05:18.030 --> 00:05:20.120
Why them?

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:22.510
I got rid of all the evidence!

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:27.270
Anyway, I have to lose them.

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:29.720
Change of plans.

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:31.240
Go over there.

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:51.000
They're here.

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:54.020
But how did they find out?

00:05:57.030 --> 00:05:58.230
So?

00:05:58.230 --> 00:06:00.530
All right.  He's all alone right now.

00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:01.510
This is our chance!

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:07.010
Oh my!  The new Japanese sauce 
noodles has been released!

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:10.790
And that's the re-release 
of the rare Yellow Weasel!

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:17.660
What are you doing?

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:20.390
What do you want with me?

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:24.080
You stole our program!

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:25.730
Give it back!

00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:28.190
What are you talking about?

00:06:28.190 --> 00:06:29.420
Don't act dumb!

00:06:29.420 --> 00:06:32.700
We found your fingerprint in our garage!

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:33.360
Fingerprint?

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:34.470
That's right!

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:37.800
I'm going to get revenge for my cup noodles!

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:40.410
Was it when...

00:06:47.850 --> 00:06:52.620
It was a new product, so I couldn't 
resist.  That was my downfall!

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:56.090
But I'm going to escape.

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:59.890
I have no clue what you're talking about.

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:06.380
Until next time!

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:08.390
You!

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:17.480
He always escapes quickly!

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:18.400
After him!

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:31.490
Where is he?

00:07:31.490 --> 00:07:33.100
Where did he go?

00:07:34.280 --> 00:07:35.200
What?

00:07:38.170 --> 00:07:39.650
There are two of him?

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:41.530
What's going on?

00:07:44.110 --> 00:07:45.660
After them!

00:07:58.890 --> 00:08:00.450
Let's split up!

00:08:07.610 --> 00:08:10.360
Damn!  It's hard to grab him!

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:16.530
All right!  He went into the bathroom!

00:08:17.020 --> 00:08:18.730
We win!

00:08:18.730 --> 00:08:20.340
We caught you!

00:08:27.090 --> 00:08:28.720
He vanished?

00:08:35.630 --> 00:08:37.150
Stop!

00:08:42.070 --> 00:08:44.230
What?  Can it be?

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:57.070
What's this?

00:08:58.250 --> 00:09:03.370
He tricked us by attaching a hologram 
projector on this remote control car.

00:09:03.370 --> 00:09:06.060
The other one is probably the same.

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:08.430
Then the real one is...

00:09:57.080 --> 00:09:58.710
The exchange will happen here.

00:09:58.710 --> 00:09:59.830
What should we do?

00:09:59.830 --> 00:10:00.710
Should we wait for everyone?

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:01.690
No.

00:10:01.690 --> 00:10:05.180
I already transmitted our 
location to Jack and Crow.

00:10:05.180 --> 00:10:09.200
Unless we catch him in the 
act, he won't confess.

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:10.720
Let's follow him.

00:10:36.750 --> 00:10:38.030
Sheesh...

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:41.400
Why do I have to act like a thief?

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:45.810
It was much easier when 
Director Godwin was in charge.

00:10:54.130 --> 00:10:56.130
You're late, you stupid clown!

00:10:58.300 --> 00:11:01.330
I'm very sorry!

00:11:01.330 --> 00:11:04.070
Annoying mice were chasing me.

00:11:04.590 --> 00:11:08.010
But I eluded them, so don't worry.

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:12.320
Here's the program.

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:16.720
Well done for a clown.

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:17.950
Congratulations.

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:20.320
It was difficult.

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:23.320
As the Public Maintenance 
Department's Vice Director,

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:26.530
I couldn't use my workers because 
this mission was secret.

00:11:27.310 --> 00:11:33.090
I had to sneak into their 
home personally to steal it.

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:39.630
As a reward, can you tell me something?

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:42.650
Tell you what?

00:11:42.650 --> 00:11:48.150
What are you going to use their program for?

00:11:51.990 --> 00:11:54.160
Don't stick your nose 
where it doesn't belong.

00:11:54.160 --> 00:11:57.130
It's better for you if you don't know.

00:12:04.860 --> 00:12:06.540
It's them.

00:12:07.190 --> 00:12:09.010
No way!

00:12:09.010 --> 00:12:10.190
You fool.

00:12:10.190 --> 00:12:11.320
You were followed.

00:12:11.320 --> 00:12:13.780
Excuse me!

00:12:16.790 --> 00:12:20.550
They're here to retrieve the program.

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:22.520
In that case...

00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:41.070
What are they building in this factory?

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:44.040
It's like the inside of a spaceship.

00:12:44.040 --> 00:12:45.160
Yeah.

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:48.780
I've never seen such a 
technologically-advanced factory.

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:51.840
A security camera!

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:55.390
That's...

00:12:55.390 --> 00:12:55.980
Hurry!

00:12:55.980 --> 00:12:56.650
Okay!

00:13:03.150 --> 00:13:03.850
Bruno!

00:13:03.850 --> 00:13:04.890
I can't make it!

00:13:04.890 --> 00:13:05.700
Bruno!

00:13:06.080 --> 00:13:07.700
Are you okay, Bruno?

00:13:07.700 --> 00:13:09.240
I'm sorry, Yusei.

00:13:09.240 --> 00:13:10.400
I'm fine!

00:13:10.400 --> 00:13:11.480
I see.

00:13:11.870 --> 00:13:13.800
I'm going to keep going.

00:13:13.800 --> 00:13:14.900
Okay.

00:13:14.900 --> 00:13:16.760
I'll call Jack!

00:13:16.760 --> 00:13:18.110
Thanks!

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:26.550
You!

00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:38.560
The only thing left to do 
is install the program.

00:13:40.410 --> 00:13:43.070
I need you to stall for time.

00:14:03.800 --> 00:14:05.890
Give back our program!

00:14:05.890 --> 00:14:07.180
Program?

00:14:07.180 --> 00:14:10.700
What are you talking about?

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:12.130
Stop acting dumb!

00:14:12.130 --> 00:14:14.320
Weren't you meeting someone here?

00:14:14.320 --> 00:14:18.570
No, I'm here to take a tour of the factory.

00:14:18.570 --> 00:14:19.620
You!

00:14:29.730 --> 00:14:30.850
What's that?

00:14:35.400 --> 00:14:38.590
100% match with recorded data.

00:14:38.590 --> 00:14:40.560
Yusei Fudo confirmed.

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:50.560
The factory is completely locked down.

00:14:50.920 --> 00:14:55.710
If you don't defeat me in a duel, 
the lock won't be released.

00:14:55.710 --> 00:14:56.850
What?

00:14:56.850 --> 00:15:03.810
Yusei Fudo, I inputted your battle 
history data into the guard robot.

00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:07.280
It's an excellent opponent to stall for time.

00:15:10.270 --> 00:15:12.650
Is this the right direction?

00:15:14.990 --> 00:15:17.810
If a door's locked, then unlock it!

00:15:21.380 --> 00:15:24.320
If I don't defeat it, the 
lock won't be released?

00:15:24.320 --> 00:15:25.800
That's right!

00:15:25.800 --> 00:15:28.190
We're in the same boat!

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:31.440
It's your choice whether 
we move forward or back!

00:15:31.440 --> 00:15:36.440
Yusei Fudo's probability 
of accepting this duel...

00:15:36.930 --> 00:15:38.580
100%.

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:42.010
Defeat it, Yusei Fudo!

00:15:42.010 --> 00:15:43.250
Be quiet!

00:15:46.810 --> 00:15:51.270
Yeager is playing dumb, but this 
place is heavily fortified.

00:15:51.270 --> 00:15:54.480
That means there's something 
hidden deep within the factory!

00:15:55.410 --> 00:15:59.440
Fine!  I accept this duel!

00:16:00.380 --> 00:16:01.710
Duel!

00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:09.020
Where am I?

00:16:10.040 --> 00:16:12.480
This place isn't for you.

00:16:12.480 --> 00:16:14.180
Who are you?

00:16:16.710 --> 00:16:17.890
You're...

00:16:22.350 --> 00:16:24.350
I won't let anyone interfere.

00:16:28.270 --> 00:16:33.070
I'll give you the greatest engine program.

00:16:51.410 --> 00:16:59.230
Until the mightiest Riding Roids come to life, 
Yusei Fudo will enjoy how I'm stalling for time!

00:17:15.350 --> 00:17:17.850
I can't waste time here.

00:17:17.850 --> 00:17:19.680
I'll finish this in an instant!

00:17:20.290 --> 00:17:21.600
My turn!

00:17:21.600 --> 00:17:24.770
I activate the spell card 
One for One from my hand!

00:17:24.770 --> 00:17:27.970
By sending Speed Warrior to the graveyard,

00:17:27.970 --> 00:17:32.060
I can Special Summon Level 1 Level 
Eater from my deck in defense position!

00:17:32.440 --> 00:17:36.030
Next, I Normal Summon Junk 
Synchron from my hand!

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:41.300
Due to Junk Synchron's effect,

00:17:41.300 --> 00:17:44.760
I Special Summon Speed Warrior from 
my graveyard in defense position!

00:17:46.130 --> 00:17:50.310
Level 3 Junk Synchron tunes 
Level 2 Speed Warrior!

00:17:56.490 --> 00:17:59.920
The stars come together 
to call forth a new power!

00:17:59.920 --> 00:18:01.730
Become the path that lights the way!

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:04.290
Synchro Summon!

00:18:04.290 --> 00:18:06.530
Come forth, Junk Warrior!

00:18:10.590 --> 00:18:13.080
A Synchro Summon on the first turn!

00:18:13.080 --> 00:18:15.230
That was fast!

00:18:15.230 --> 00:18:16.330
I'm not done!

00:18:16.330 --> 00:18:19.630
Junk Warrior gains attack points 
equal to the attack points

00:18:19.630 --> 00:18:22.470
of Level 2-or-below monsters on my field!

00:18:22.920 --> 00:18:26.690
It gains Level Eater's 600 attack points!

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:31.420
I set one card and end my turn.

00:18:31.420 --> 00:18:33.160
I see!

00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:37.430
He Special Summoned Level Eater at the 
beginning because he anticipated this!

00:18:37.430 --> 00:18:38.800
Well done!

00:18:41.560 --> 00:18:46.380
Probability of Synchro Summoning 
on the first turn was 45%.

00:18:46.380 --> 00:18:48.110
My data expected this.

00:18:48.110 --> 00:18:50.310
What is it calculating?

00:18:50.310 --> 00:18:57.780
As a counter, I will stop his high-Level 
monsters on the second turn.

00:18:57.780 --> 00:18:58.520
What?

00:18:58.730 --> 00:19:00.140
My turn.

00:19:02.270 --> 00:19:06.220
I activate the Continuous Spell 
Level Limit - Area B from my hand.

00:19:06.860 --> 00:19:10.860
Due to Level Limit - Area B's 
effect, all Level 4-and-higher

00:19:10.860 --> 00:19:14.840
monsters on the field switch 
to defense position!

00:19:16.520 --> 00:19:23.250
He went through all that trouble to summon 
the Synchro Monster, but it can't attack!

00:19:24.870 --> 00:19:28.470
I set three cards and end my turn.

00:19:30.680 --> 00:19:34.100
It's using a lock deck to 
lengthen the duel's duration.

00:19:34.100 --> 00:19:36.120
It's stalling for time.

00:19:36.120 --> 00:19:39.140
But it has no monsters on its field.

00:19:39.370 --> 00:19:44.630
Even if Level Limit - Area B is active, I 
can attack it with Level 3-or-below monsters.

00:19:44.630 --> 00:19:45.530
Therefore...

00:19:45.720 --> 00:19:47.000
My turn!

00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:49.460
I activate the trap card Graceful Revival!

00:19:49.460 --> 00:19:56.010
I select one Level 2-or-below monster in my 
graveyard and Special Summon it in attack position!

00:19:57.690 --> 00:20:00.730
Speed Warrior resurrects from the graveyard!

00:20:01.530 --> 00:20:10.020
Probability of Yusei Fudo Special Summoning a 
monster to counteract Level Limit - Area B was 98%.

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:10.750
What?

00:20:10.930 --> 00:20:15.300
At this moment, the Counter 
Trap Malfunction activates.

00:20:15.300 --> 00:20:19.100
By paying 500 life points, your 
trap card's activation is negated,

00:20:19.100 --> 00:20:21.730
and it's returned to its original state.

00:20:23.380 --> 00:20:29.940
Since I countered your card, I Special 
Summon Lock Dragon in defense position.

00:20:30.550 --> 00:20:36.520
I can Special Summon Lock Dragon when I 
use a Counter Trap to negate your effect.

00:20:36.520 --> 00:20:42.180
When it's on the field in defense 
position, Special Summons are negated.

00:20:42.180 --> 00:20:43.280
What?

00:20:44.310 --> 00:20:47.370
Synchro Summons are completely stopped!

00:20:47.370 --> 00:20:52.130
He won't be able to summon his 
ace monster Stardust Dragon!

00:20:52.320 --> 00:20:57.010
It not only anticipated my fast start, 
but also that I'd try to stop its trap.

00:20:57.010 --> 00:20:59.150
It has the momentum.

00:20:59.880 --> 00:21:03.240
This card has also activated.

00:21:04.390 --> 00:21:07.170
The Continuous Trap Counter Force.

00:21:08.290 --> 00:21:14.470
Every time a Counter Trap activates, 
Counter Force gains one counter.

00:21:15.680 --> 00:21:18.830
By removing this card from 
play, you take damage

00:21:18.830 --> 00:21:22.280
equal to the number of counters 
multiplied by 1000 points.

00:21:26.200 --> 00:21:29.140
At this rate, he can't attack!

00:21:29.140 --> 00:21:33.170
He can't do anything but watch 
the counters accumulate!

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:38.110
It calculated everything 
that I'm going to do?

00:22:09.490 --> 00:22:14.170
The small cliff floats on the Milky Way

00:22:14.170 --> 00:22:19.180
The sights I see are different 
than what I imagined

00:22:19.460 --> 00:22:24.080
Were you able to move on from the past?

00:22:24.080 --> 00:22:29.090
The answer isn't no, but 
there's something missing

00:22:29.290 --> 00:22:33.960
The cruel god tests us

00:22:34.260 --> 00:22:40.900
Let's fill the emptiness 
and head to the next stage

00:22:40.900 --> 00:22:44.770
If you ask me "What's our relationship?"

00:22:44.770 --> 00:22:50.640
We're more than friends... 
but that's not quite right

00:22:50.810 --> 00:22:54.560
Bond is the proper word

00:22:54.560 --> 00:23:00.540
As we fight, we understand each other

00:23:00.540 --> 00:23:03.510
"Where are you right now?"  "On Earth"

00:23:03.510 --> 00:23:05.740
Because I'm not an astronaut

00:23:05.740 --> 00:23:10.420
I have no problems when 
I'm below the ozone layer

00:23:10.710 --> 00:23:13.280
"I know, I'm coming right away."

00:23:13.280 --> 00:23:16.750
You want to party until the morning

00:23:16.750 --> 00:23:19.990
At our special place
